2:## N5b. The draw layer of a world: every pack is SIMULATED at the origin of its own physics space (N2), and DRAWN at
3:## its plot. This node never touches a physics body, a transform of a pack node, or anything a state hash reads.
5:## The stage rule: the stage pack (the one the player is in) is drawn natively, at zero offset. Every other pack, the
6:## landscape and the far stand-ins are drawn at `rel_i = plot_stage^-1 * plot_i`. `set_stage(i)` re-bases all of it once.
8:## Two mechanisms, chosen with `mech` (see DRAW.md for the measurement that decided):
9:##   "a"  offset in the shaders: `instance uniform vec4 tl_plot` (xyz offset, w yaw) of every style shader, set once on
10:##        each GeometryInstance3D of a pack. Whatever is not style geometry (lights, a pack's own material) is mirrored.
11:##   "b"  mirror instances: one RenderingServer instance per visual with the SAME base (mesh, multimesh, light), at
12:##        `rel * node.global_transform`; the node's own instance is hidden on the server. Moved nodes are re-sent in
13:##        `_process` (one comparison per visual per frame).
14:## Culling for "a" (`cull`): the engine culls with the box of the place where the pack is simulated, so each instance
15:## needs help. "auto" (kept): an instance that stands still gets a `custom_aabb` around its drawn place, once; an
16:## instance under a moving body, a skeleton or a particle emitter is never culled (`extra_cull_margin`); a slow
17:## round-robin check (WATCH instances per pack per frame) moves any "still" instance that a script turned after all
18:## into the never-culled class. "aabb" refreshes every box every frame (exact, one comparison per instance per frame),
19:## "margin" never culls anything of a non-stage pack.
21:## Far packs (`far_mode` "auto" beyond `far_dist`, or "all"; in a scheduled world the tiers `backdrop` and `ledger`):
22:## the pack's holder is hidden and one of two merged PICTURES of it is shown instead (P6, draw/FAR.md):
23:##   "mid"  the venue's large forms (instances shorter than `mid_min` dropped) plus signs of life: one mark per moving
24:##          body (a box in the body's colour, one multimesh per pack, moved when the pack ticks), a copy of its smoke,
25:##          a few of its lights;
26:##   "far"  a silhouette: only forms of at least `far_min`, its own ground re-meshed coarsely, normals leaning up so
27:##          it is drawn in flat tones with one outline; the marks stay (larger), so the picture still moves.
28:## Which of the two is decided per frame by the camera's distance to the plot edge (`picture_far_m`, with a margin
29:## both ways). "still" is N5b's stand-in (everything above 1.2 m, nothing moving), kept for comparison:
30:## the env variable TL_DRAW_PICTURE=still|mid|far forces one picture on every far pack.
