90:## Once per drawn frame and pack: the score on its boards and the marks of its moving bodies follow the pack's OWN
91:## ticks (a backdrop game ticks one world tick in `slice`, so its picture moves at that pace); a far pack changes
92:## between its two pictures when the camera crosses the threshold. Reads the pack, never writes it.
93:func _life(e: Dictionary, _i: int) -> void:
